  "source": "printf '%s' '<stored bytes>' | sha256sum; openssl dgst -sha256 agrees. The checkout bytes: printf '%s' '{\"id\":\"chk_1001\",\"total\":{\"currency\":\"USD\",\"amount\":27999}}' | base64. The reference is Wix's documented providerTransactionId example. fixed.agreement is a stated input. expiresAt: date -u -d @1790000900. The agreement URL is https://<the tenant's first host>/agreement/ followed by fixed.agreementTokens[0], 16 random bytes in base64url without padding (head -c 16 /dev/urandom | basenc --base64url | tr -d '='): a path from a random token, never from the hash, which a connector places exactly as issue returns it; the agreement transaction is a stated input, recorded before the report. Once the agreement is recorded, the pattern's statement names it: sed 's/<network>/eip155:84532/; s/<transaction>/<the agreement transaction>/'. The link is storageBase followed by fixed.linkTokens[0], 16 random bytes in base64url without padding (head -c 16 /dev/urandom | basenc --base64url | tr -d '='): a path from a random token, never from the hash. legalContextUrl and legal_context_url are the same link."
